{"formatVersion":1,"translationId":"BSB","textDirection":"ltr","bookId":"OBA","bookName":"Obadiah","chapters":[{"number":1,"lastVerse":21,"verses":[{"number":1,"lines":[{"text":"This is the vision of Obadiah:"},{"text":"This is what the Lord GOD says about Edom—","poem":1},{"text":"We have heard a message from the LORD;","poem":1},{"text":"an envoy has been sent among the nations","poem":2},{"text":"to say, “Rise up,","poem":1},{"text":"and let us go to battle against her!”—","poem":2}]},{"number":2,"lines":[{"text":"“Behold, I will make you small among the nations;","poem":1},{"text":"you will be deeply despised.","poem":2}]},{"number":3,"lines":[{"text":"The pride of your heart has deceived you,","poem":1},{"text":"O dwellers in the clefts of the rocks","poem":2},{"text":"whose habitation is the heights,","poem":2},{"text":"who say in your heart,","poem":1},{"text":"‘Who can bring me down to the ground?’","poem":2}]},{"number":4,"lines":[{"text":"Though you soar like the eagle","poem":1},{"text":"and make your nest among the stars,","poem":2},{"text":"even from there I will bring you down,”","poem":2},{"text":"declares the LORD."}]},{"number":5,"lines":[{"text":"“If thieves came to you,","poem":1},{"text":"if robbers by night—","poem":2},{"text":"oh, how you will be ruined—","poem":1},{"text":"would they not steal only what they wanted?","poem":2},{"text":"If grape gatherers came to you,","poem":1},{"text":"would they not leave some gleanings?","poem":2}]},{"number":6,"lines":[{"text":"But how Esau will be pillaged,","poem":1},{"text":"his hidden treasures sought out!","poem":2}]},{"number":7,"lines":[{"text":"All the men allied with you","poem":1},{"text":"will drive you to the border;","poem":2},{"text":"the men at peace with you","poem":1},{"text":"will deceive and overpower you.","poem":2},{"text":"Those who eat your bread","poem":1},{"text":"will set a trap for you","poem":2},{"text":"without your awareness of it.","poem":2}]},{"number":8,"lines":[{"text":"In that day, declares the LORD,","poem":1},{"text":"will I not destroy the wise men of Edom","poem":2},{"text":"and the men of understanding","poem":1},{"text":"in the mountains of Esau?","poem":2}]},{"number":9,"lines":[{"text":"Then your mighty men, O Teman,","poem":1},{"text":"will be terrified,","poem":2},{"text":"so that everyone in the mountains of Esau","poem":1},{"text":"will be cut down in the slaughter.","poem":2}]},{"number":10,"lines":[{"text":"Because of the violence against your brother Jacob,","poem":1},{"text":"you will be covered with shame","poem":2},{"text":"and cut off forever.","poem":2}]},{"number":11,"lines":[{"text":"On the day you stood aloof","poem":1},{"text":"while strangers carried off his wealth","poem":2},{"text":"and foreigners entered his gate","poem":1},{"text":"and cast lots for Jerusalem,","poem":2},{"text":"you were just like one of them.","poem":2}]},{"number":12,"lines":[{"text":"But you should not gloat in that day,","poem":1},{"text":"your brother’s day of misfortune,","poem":2},{"text":"nor rejoice over the people of Judah","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their destruction,","poem":2},{"text":"nor boast proudly","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their distress.","poem":2}]},{"number":13,"lines":[{"text":"You should not enter the gate of My people","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their disaster,","poem":2},{"text":"nor gloat over their affliction","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their disaster,","poem":2},{"text":"nor loot their wealth","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their disaster.","poem":2}]},{"number":14,"lines":[{"text":"Nor should you stand at the crossroads","poem":1},{"text":"to cut off their fugitives,","poem":2},{"text":"nor deliver up their survivors","poem":1},{"text":"in the day of their distress.","poem":2}]},{"number":15,"lines":[{"text":"For the Day of the LORD is near","poem":1},{"text":"for all the nations.","poem":2},{"text":"As you have done, it will be done to you;","poem":1},{"text":"your recompense will return upon your own head.","poem":2}]},{"number":16,"lines":[{"text":"For as you drank on My holy mountain,","poem":1},{"text":"so all the nations will drink continually.","poem":2},{"text":"They will drink and gulp it down;","poem":1},{"text":"they will be as if they had never existed.","poem":2}]},{"number":17,"lines":[{"text":"But on Mount Zion there will be deliverance,","poem":1},{"text":"and it will be holy,","poem":2},{"text":"and the house of Jacob","poem":1},{"text":"will reclaim their possession.","poem":2}]},{"number":18,"lines":[{"text":"Then the house of Jacob will be a blazing fire,","poem":1},{"text":"and the house of Joseph a burning flame;","poem":2},{"text":"but the house of Esau will be stubble—","poem":1},{"text":"Jacob will set it ablaze and consume it.","poem":2},{"text":"Therefore no survivor will remain","poem":1},{"text":"from the house of Esau.”","poem":2},{"text":"For the LORD has spoken."}]},{"number":19,"lines":[{"text":"Those from the Negev will possess the mountains of Esau;","poem":1},{"text":"those from the foothills will possess the land of the Philistines.","poem":2},{"text":"They will occupy the fields of Ephraim and Samaria,","poem":1},{"text":"and Benjamin will possess Gilead.","poem":2}]},{"number":20,"lines":[{"text":"And the exiles of this host of the Israelites","poem":1},{"text":"will possess the land of the Canaanites as far as Zarephath;","poem":2},{"text":"and the exiles from Jerusalem who are in Sepharad","poem":1},{"text":"will possess the cities of the Negev.","poem":2}]},{"number":21,"lines":[{"text":"The deliverers will ascend Mount Zion","poem":1},{"text":"to rule over the mountains of Esau.","poem":2},{"text":"And the kingdom will belong to the LORD.","poem":1}]}]}]}
